.TH CHERUBSH-READLINE 3 "August 2026" "CherubSH" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
cherubsh-readline \- Readline 8.3 and History compatibility libraries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <readline/readline.h>
#include <readline/history.h>

char *line = readline("prompt> ");
.fi
.PP
Compile with pkg-config:
.nf
cc client.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs readline history)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The CherubSH development archive provides C-compatible Readline and History
libraries, public headers, shared-library links, static archives, and pkg-config
files. The compatibility target is GNU Readline 8.3 patch 3.
.PP
Applications own the string returned by
.BR readline ()
and release it with
.BR free (3).
History entries and callbacks follow the ownership rules declared by the
installed Readline headers.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I include/readline
Readline and History public headers.
.TP
.I lib/libreadline.so
Readline shared-library linker name.
.TP
.I lib/libhistory.so
History shared-library linker name.
.TP
.I lib/pkgconfig/readline.pc
Readline compiler and linker metadata.
.TP
.I lib/pkgconfig/history.pc
History compiler and linker metadata.
.SH INSTALLATION
Use the installer from the versioned Readline development archive. It supports
an absolute prefix, DESTDIR staging, component installation, and uninstall.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cherubsh (1),
.BR readline (3),
.BR history (3)
